## Fully Automated CI/CD Pipeline on AWS with Blue/Green Deployments

### 1. Design Overview & Architecture

The solution implements a complete CI/CD pipeline using **AWS** as the cloud provider, **GitHub Actions** for orchestration, **Terraform** for infrastructure as code, **Amazon ECS (Fargate)** for serverless container hosting, and **AWS CodeDeploy** for automated blue/green deployments. The pipeline monitors a source code repository (`main` branch), and on every new commit:

1. **Builds** a container image, runs unit tests.
2. **Provisions an ephemeral, isolated staging environment** using Terraform – each commit gets its own ECS service, target group, and ALB routing rule.
3. **Deploys the new container** to that staging environment.
4. **Runs integration/smoke tests** against the staging URL.
5. **Promotes to production** via a CodeDeploy blue/green deployment (zero‑downtime traffic shifting).
6. **Verifies the deployment** with smoke tests against production.
7. **Sends notifications** at each stage (success/failure).
8. **Destroys the ephemeral staging environment** after promotion (optional).

All infrastructure is immutable and defined in Terraform. Serverless and managed services are preferred everywhere (Fargate, ECR, CodeDeploy, SNS, Secrets Manager). Auditing is built‑in: every resource is tagged with the Git commit SHA, image tags match the commit, CodeDeploy logs all deployment events, and CloudTrail captures API actions. Secrets are stored in AWS Secrets Manager and injected securely into containers.

**Architecture diagram (logical flow):**
```
[GitHub (main)]
    │
    ▼
[GitHub Actions Runner]
    │
    ├─[Build]───> [ECR] (image:sha-abc123)
    ├─[Unit tests]
    │
    ├─[Terraform apply]───> [Staging ALB] + [ECS (Fargate) service “sha-abc123”] (isolated)
    ├─[Integration tests]───> https://abc123.staging.example.com
    │
    ├─[CodeDeploy trigger]───> [Production ECS Blue/Green service] (new green task set)
    ├─[Smoke tests on production]
    └─[SNS / Slack notifications]
```

---

### 2. Infrastructure as Code (Terraform)

All shared, persistent infrastructure is defined in the `base-infra` workspace. Per‑commit ephemeral staging resources are created by a reusable Terraform **module** that the pipeline instantiates with a unique commit SHA.

#### 2.1. Base Infrastructure (`main.tf`)

```hcl
# main.tf – Base persistent resources (VPC, ECR, ALBs, ECS cluster, CodeDeploy, etc.)

provider "aws" {
  region = var.aws_region
}

terraform {
  backend "s3" {
    bucket         = var.state_bucket
    key            = "base-infra/terraform.tfstate"
    region         = var.aws_region
    encrypt        = true
    dynamodb_table = "terraform-locks"
  }
}

# ── Networking ──────────────────────────────────────────────
module "vpc" {
  source  = "terraform-aws-modules/vpc/aws"
  version = "5.0.0"

  name = "myapp-vpc"
  cidr = "10.0.0.0/16"

  azs             = ["us-east-1a", "us-east-1b"]
  private_subnets = ["10.0.1.0/24", "10.0.2.0/24"]
  public_subnets  = ["10.0.101.0/24", "10.0.102.0/24"]

  enable_nat_gateway = true
  single_nat_gateway = false
}

# ── ECR Repository ─────────────────────────────────────────
resource "aws_ecr_repository" "app" {
  name                 = var.app_name
  image_tag_mutability = "IMMUTABLE"
  image_scanning_configuration {
    scan_on_push = true
  }
}

# ── ECS Cluster (Fargate) ──────────────────────────────────
resource "aws_ecs_cluster" "main" {
  name = "${var.app_name}-cluster"
  setting {
    name  = "containerInsights"
    value = "enabled"
  }
}

# ── Security Groups ────────────────────────────────────────
resource "aws_security_group" "alb" {
  name        = "${var.app_name}-alb-sg"
  description = "ALB public access"
  vpc_id      = module.vpc.vpc_id

  ingress {
    from_port   = 443
    to_port     = 443
    protocol    = "tcp"
    cidr_blocks = ["0.0.0.0/0"]
  }
  ingress {
    from_port   = 80
    to_port     = 80
    protocol    = "tcp"
    cidr_blocks = ["0.0.0.0/0"]
  }
  egress {
    from_port   = 0
    to_port     = 0
    protocol    = "-1"
    cidr_blocks = ["0.0.0.0/0"]
  }
}

resource "aws_security_group" "ecs" {
  name        = "${var.app_name}-ecs-sg"
  description = "ECS task access"
  vpc_id      = module.vpc.vpc_id

  ingress {
    from_port       = 80
    to_port         = 80
    protocol        = "tcp"
    security_groups = [aws_security_group.alb.id]
  }
  egress {
    from_port   = 0
    to_port     = 0
    protocol    = "-1"
    cidr_blocks = ["0.0.0.0/0"]
  }
}

# ── Load Balancers ─────────────────────────────────────────

# Production ALB
resource "aws_lb" "prod" {
  name               = "${var.app_name}-prod-alb"
  internal           = false
  load_balancer_type = "application"
  security_groups    = [aws_security_group.alb.id]
  subnets            = module.vpc.public_subnets
}

# Staging ALB (shared for all ephemeral environments)
resource "aws_lb" "staging" {
  name               = "${var.app_name}-staging-alb"
  internal           = false
  load_balancer_type = "application"
  security_groups    = [aws_security_group.alb.id]
  subnets            = module.vpc.public_subnets
}

# Production HTTPS listener
resource "aws_lb_listener" "prod" {
  load_balancer_arn = aws_lb.prod.arn
  port              = 443
  protocol          = "HTTPS"
  ssl_policy        = "ELBSecurityPolicy-2016-08"
  certificate_arn   = var.prod_acm_certificate_arn

  default_action {
    type             = "forward"
    target_group_arn = aws_lb_target_group.prod_blue.arn
  }
}

# Staging HTTPS listener (default 404, actual routes added per commit)
resource "aws_lb_listener" "staging" {
  load_balancer_arn = aws_lb.staging.arn
  port              = 443
  protocol          = "HTTPS"
  ssl_policy        = "ELBSecurityPolicy-2016-08"
  certificate_arn   = var.staging_acm_certificate_arn   # *.staging.example.com

  default_action {
    type = "fixed-response"
    fixed_response {
      content_type = "text/plain"
      message_body = "No staging environment for this commit"
      status_code  = "404"
    }
  }
}

# Production Target Groups (blue/green)
resource "aws_lb_target_group" "prod_blue" {
  name        = "${var.app_name}-blue-tg"
  port        = 80
  protocol    = "HTTP"
  vpc_id      = module.vpc.vpc_id
  target_type = "ip"

  health_check {
    path                = "/health"
    interval            = 10
    healthy_threshold   = 2
    unhealthy_threshold = 3
    timeout             = 5
    matcher             = "200"
  }
}

resource "aws_lb_target_group" "prod_green" {
  name        = "${var.app_name}-green-tg"
  port        = 80
  protocol    = "HTTP"
  vpc_id      = module.vpc.vpc_id
  target_type = "ip"

  health_check {
    path                = "/health"
    interval            = 10
    healthy_threshold   = 2
    unhealthy_threshold = 3
    timeout             = 5
    matcher             = "200"
  }
}

# ── ECS Task Definition (initial production) ───────────────
resource "aws_ecs_task_definition" "prod" {
  family                   = "${var.app_name}-prod"
  network_mode             = "awsvpc"
  requires_compatibilities = ["FARGATE"]
  cpu                      = var.task_cpu
  memory                   = var.task_memory
  execution_role_arn       = aws_iam_role.ecs_execution.arn
  task_role_arn            = aws_iam_role.ecs_task.arn
  container_definitions    = jsonencode([
    {
      name  = var.app_name
      image = "${aws_ecr_repository.app.repository_url}:latest"   # placeholder
      portMappings = [{ containerPort = 80 }]
      secrets = [
        {
          name      = "DB_PASSWORD"
          valueFrom = aws_secretsmanager_secret.db_password.arn
        }
      ]
      logConfiguration = {
        logDriver = "awslogs"
        options = {
          awslogs-group         = aws_cloudwatch_log_group.ecs.name
          awslogs-region        = var.aws_region
          awslogs-stream-prefix = "prod"
        }
      }
      healthCheck = {
        command     = ["CMD-SHELL", "curl -f http://localhost/health || exit 1"]
        interval    = 10
        timeout     = 5
        retries     = 3
        startPeriod = 30
      }
    }
  ])
}

# Production ECS Service with CodeDeploy controller
resource "aws_ecs_service" "prod" {
  name                              = "${var.app_name}-prod-service"
  cluster                           = aws_ecs_cluster.main.id
  task_definition                   = aws_ecs_task_definition.prod.arn
  desired_count                     = var.prod_desired_count
  launch_type                       = "FARGATE"
  health_check_grace_period_seconds = 60

  deployment_controller {
    type = "CODE_DEPLOY"
  }

  network_configuration {
    subnets          = module.vpc.private_subnets
    security_groups  = [aws_security_group.ecs.id]
    assign_public_ip = false
  }

  load_balancer {
    target_group_arn = aws_lb_target_group.prod_blue.arn
    container_name   = var.app_name
    container_port   = 80
  }

  lifecycle {
    ignore_changes = [task_definition, load_balancer]
  }
}

# ── CodeDeploy Application and Deployment Group ───────────
resource "aws_codedeploy_app" "app" {
  compute_platform = "ECS"
  name             = var.app_name
}

resource "aws_codedeploy_deployment_group" "prod" {
  app_name               = aws_codedeploy_app.app.name
  deployment_group_name  = "${var.app_name}-prod-dg"
  service_role_arn       = aws_iam_role.codedeploy.arn
  deployment_config_name = "CodeDeployDefault.ECSLinear10PercentEvery1Minute"  # Can be customised

  blue_green_deployment_config {
    deployment_ready_option {
      action_on_timeout = "CONTINUE_DEPLOYMENT"
    }
    terminate_blue_instances_on_deployment_success {
      action                           = "TERMINATE"
      termination_wait_time_in_minutes = 5
    }
  }

  ecs_service {
    cluster_name = aws_ecs_cluster.main.name
    service_name = aws_ecs_service.prod.name
  }

  load_balancer_info {
    target_group_pair_info {
      prod_traffic_route {
        listener_arns = [aws_lb_listener.prod.arn]
      }
      target_group { name = aws_lb_target_group.prod_blue.name }
      target_group { name = aws_lb_target_group.prod_green.name }
    }
  }

  auto_rollback_configuration {
    enabled = true
    events  = ["DEPLOYMENT_FAILURE", "DEPLOYMENT_STOP_ON_ALARM"]
  }

  # Optional: trigger a Lambda to run post‑traffic validation tests
  # trigger_configuration { ... }
}

# ── CloudWatch Logs ───────────────────────────────────────
resource "aws_cloudwatch_log_group" "ecs" {
  name              = "/ecs/${var.app_name}"
  retention_in_days = 30
}

# ── SNS Notifications ─────────────────────────────────────
resource "aws_sns_topic" "pipeline" {
  name = "${var.app_name}-pipeline-events"
  # Subscribe via email, Lambda, or Slack
}

# ── IAM Roles (simplified) ────────────────────────────────
resource "aws_iam_role" "ecs_execution" {
  name = "${var.app_name}-ecs-execution"
  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [{
      Effect = "Allow"
      Principal = { Service = "ecs-tasks.amazonaws.com" }
      Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
    }]
  })
  # Attach managed policies for ECR pull, Secrets Manager, CloudWatch logs
  managed_policy_arns = [
    "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AmazonECSTaskExecutionRolePolicy",
    "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/SecretsManagerReadWrite"   # restrict in production
  ]
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "ecs_task" {
  name = "${var.app_name}-ecs-task"
  assume_role_policy = data.aws_iam_policy_document.ecs_task_assume.json
  # Add policies for app‑specific AWS resources
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "codedeploy" {
  name = "${var.app_name}-codedeploy"
  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [{
      Effect = "Allow"
      Principal = { Service = "codedeploy.amazonaws.com" }
      Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
    }]
  })
  # Attach AWSCodeDeployRoleForECS
  managed_policy_arns = [
    "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AWSCodeDeployRoleForECS"
  ]
}

# GitHub Actions OIDC role
resource "aws_iam_role" "github_actions" {
  name = "github-actions-oidc"
  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [{
      Effect = "Allow"
      Principal = { Federated = aws_iam_openid_connect_provider.github.arn }
      Action = "sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity"
      Condition = {
        StringEquals = {
          "token.actions.githubusercontent.com:sub" = "repo:${var.github_repo}:ref:refs/heads/main"
        }
      }
    }]
  })
  # Attach policies granting access to ECR, ECS, CodeDeploy, Terraform state S3, etc.
}
